{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"a80d214c06883d2c2247dd1df645ecda84f2a9b97dd6e3818c40de909454c2e7","packTokens":2810,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":240,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":700,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1550,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using their Folio3 Google account, with employee profiles and vehicle details populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking with a single action and view its status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can schedule or cancel parking releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can view availability and claim released parking on a first-come, first-served basis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and generate and email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What may Parking Administrators and Security Guards do in the web app, beyond the functions already described?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Administrators manage employee and parking records, assignments, configuration, and report recipients; guards use only the entrance indicator and existing sticker process.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may receive reports that identify employees and their unused parking, and how are recipients maintained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Parking Administrator maintains a named recipient list; only those recipients receive the report.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Which source is authoritative for employee profiles, dedicated-parking assignments, and registered vehicles when an employee signs in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the corporate directory for employee details and an administrator-maintained parking assignment and vehicle list.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"For an employee with multiple registered vehicles, what counts as parking utilization when any one of their plates is detected entering that day?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Count the allocation as used if any vehicle registered to that employee is detected.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How long should parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events be retained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply Folio3's existing records-retention policy to these records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"What makes an employee without dedicated parking eligible to claim a released space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any active Folio3 employee without a dedicated assignment who has at least one registered vehicle may claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Can a temporary parking user cancel a claim after successfully claiming a space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Claims cannot be cancelled by the user once confirmed.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"If a dedicated holder's released space has been claimed but the holder's permanently stickered vehicle arrives, how should the system treat the temporary claimant's authorization?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the temporary authorization valid; the stickered vehicle continues through the existing process even if this exceeds configured capacity.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The Folio3 Parking web app shall authenticate only active Folio3 employees using corporate Google Workspace identities, and return employee profiles populated with corporate-directory details and any administrator-maintained parking assignments, floors, and registered vehicles; non-administrators shall not access other employees’ profiles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Employees without a registered vehicle shall be required to register at least one license plate before releasing or claiming parking, and may save a vehicle with a plate and optional make, model, and color.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Parking Administrators shall have read-only access to corporate-directory employee details and be able to create, view, and update linked parking assignments and vehicle records without changing those details; other callers shall be denied those changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"A designated active Folio3 account in deployment bootstrap configuration shall receive the initial Parking Administrator role, and Parking Administrators shall be able to configure daily release time, per-floor capacities, the work calendar, named report recipients, and administrator and Security Guard roles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Every employee and administrator page shall be a responsive web page for phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow viewports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"A dedicated parking holder shall be able to release today’s reserved parking with one action, creating one release for that holder and date; parking shall show Reserved by default on expected working days without a release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"A same-day release shall become claimable at the configured daily release time in the Folio3 office time zone if submitted earlier, or immediately if submitted later.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated holders shall be able to schedule releases for one or more dates up to 30 days ahead, see scheduled releases in the release calendar, and cancel an unclaimed scheduled release; cancellation after a claim shall be rejected without changing the claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Active Folio3 employees without a dedicated assignment and with at least one registered vehicle shall be able to view claimable released parking and the current available-space count; inactive employees, dedicated holders, and employees without a registered vehicle shall not claim availability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Each released allocation shall go to only the earliest accepted eligible claim, with concurrent claims for the same last allocation allowing only one success; an accepted claim shall include its assigned floor and record the employee, date, time, and allocation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Employees shall not be able to cancel a confirmed temporary parking claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When a released allocation becomes claimable, the app shall email eligible employees without dedicated parking who have registered vehicles, using a fixed template.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"A permanently stickered vehicle’s existing sticker process shall remain unaffected, and any temporary claim already made for that date shall remain valid even if configured capacity is exceeded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"For LPR-detected cars with readable plates, the app shall verify the plate against temporary parking authorizations for that date and activate the green indicator only for a valid authorization; non-car detections shall produce no authorization response or indicator activation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"If the LPR, plate-reading service, connection, or indicator cannot verify authorization, the app shall deny temporary-parking entry and leave the green indicator inactive.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"The app shall record every successful and unsuccessful entrance verification with its timestamp, readable plate or empty plate field, result, and entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Daily utilization shall count a dedicated allocation as used when any vehicle registered to its employee is detected that day, record unused dedicated parking when none is detected, and record unused temporary parking with employee, vehicle, and date when a confirmed claimant has no registered-vehicle entry that day.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"A Monday-morning weekly reporting job in the Folio3 office time zone shall generate a report for the preceding Monday-through-Sunday week with unused dedicated and temporary parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and claim totals, and overall utilization percentage: 100 times used allocations divided by eligible allocations, or 0 percent if there are none.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Weekly report emails shall go only to addresses on the Parking Administrator’s configured named report-recipient list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Parking Administrators shall be able to filter on-screen utilization records and export the displayed records as CSV.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events shall be retained according to Folio3’s existing records-retention policy.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Phase 1 utilization functionality shall be limited to monitoring, recording, and reporting, without automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}